I'm posting this one as a tribute to xanthian. 

Playing on a PDA gives me certain advantages when I encounter an obvious
bones file, memory being the biggest one. Of course, when you get to a
familiar-looking minetown and know it's already a *double* bones file,
it's a good time to want to forget a lot of things. 

Just the previous game, I'd lost a tourist named Tikara to a giant bet;
before dying, she'd met a shopkeeper looking for another character maned
Twangi, which is a name I tended to use when I started playing elven
rangers. So there were at least two ghosts on this level, but if I was
lucky, my new gnomish ranger might have nothing else worse than a giant
bat to deal with.

Seffe's dog, Charlie, took care of the bat. The town was full of annoying
monkeys running around, but otherwise safe. The guards must have taken
care of Twangi. When I got to the coaligned temple, I knew my luck had
been phenomenally good. I bought my protection on the cheap and dropped
all the scrolls and junk I'd picked up above. Both of the scrolls I'd
price-id'd as 80 were blessed. Bu ya! I've god two old pets running
around, so now I have Charlie, Chuck, and Chas.

Hack, slash, level up to 5, uncurse a whole load of good things. Dip
five uncursed id scrolls into my only bottle of holy water, and...
identify about a third of what I have. Too bad only Itzhak is in his shop
where he belongs, because I can't price-id a single thing down here. Save
those ten spellbooks for later. 

Run upstairs to Sokoban for a BoH, then down to mine's end, turning Chuck
into a frost giant on the way, for... more spellbooks. It was the
catacombs. Back to just piles and piles of gear at the altar, and Chuck
broke out of the room I put him in, so now the priest is dead. Urgh. all
my money back and three more spell books. With an uncursed BoH I'm doing a
lot of weight and balance tradeoffs. 

But there I am, with a sack full of goodies and a (stuffing his damn self
on the watch captain) pet frost giant, ready to head back to my stash in
Soko. The watch are all gone, so what the hell, take a drink from the
fountain. You unleash a water demon! who after three rounds of Seffe
stabbing him summoned a twin, who summoned Yeenoghu. DYWYPI?

And the bones file lives on.... I think the next character who finds it
won't be so lucky. 

